{"kind":"request","text":"Claude: add bounded source preview windows so a cited line in a larger text file can be read without leaving its review. This follows the delivered #19022 navigation work; do not reopen that completed implementation. Queue after #20258, preserving active #20008 and #20112. It can use an adoption wait on #20301 before the later documentation queue.\n\nThe actual resident refuses cmd/gs/main_test.go at eligible head 07753351 (233257 bytes, 5611 newlines) with the 5000-line limit, although the review cites line726. Three source controls return ready and exact. The attached evidence records actual API responses, not a browser test. Current [preview handler](internal/service/preview.go@dfbf4089e6826810083848e56e9deff6c0faec29:41) reads a whole bounded blob then refuses every file at that line ceiling. The [preview component](ui/src/components/Preview.tsx@dfbf4089e6826810083848e56e9deff6c0faec29:92) removes the cited line before requesting content. The current [Git reader](internal/gitstore/preview.go@dfbf4089e6826810083848e56e9deff6c0faec29:52) and these two files are byte-identical to their live b2ed9266 publications. A copied excerpt let #20422 remain readable, but routine source review should not require authors to copy files into attachments.\n\nDeliver a small coherent extension: open a bounded text window containing the cited line, or the beginning without one; show actual source line numbers, the selected exact revision, and clear previous/next navigation. Keep review context and support reload, copied deep links, back/forward and close. Large readable evidence attachments should use the same bounded surface where applicable. Small-file and directory behavior must remain useful.\n\nSpecify and enforce separate limits for rendered/returned content and Git verification work. Preserve exact event/repository/head eligibility, object verification, deadlines, cancellation, concurrency limits, literal safe paths, symlink/submodule refusal and inert untrusted content. Support the observed file and a positive byte-ceiling case above512KiB within a documented finite source-read budget; do not merely raise the old whole-file ceiling or remove bounds. Files beyond that budget, invalid UTF-8/binary data and pathological lines must get an honest bounded answer, with no silent main or filesystem fallback. A bounded window is partial content and must say so.\n\nProve the actual browser path from a review link to a middle and final window, accurate line highlighting, adjacent navigation and history. Include producer/consumer controls for just-over5000-lines and just-over512KiB text, small files, empty/last/out-of-range windows, oversized single lines, UTF-8 boundaries, cancellation and rapid target changes, mismatched revisions, untrusted paths and evidence ownership. A test must fail if the cited-line window is ignored or neighboring content is presented under the wrong revision. Reuse the existing preview and routing surfaces; avoid a second inspector.\n\nUpdate architecture and reading-view/API guidance with the actual bounds in the same head, publish exact-path artifacts with one selected report, obtain independent Architecture/Security/Simplification review, ratify the verdict, seal the approved merge, push and verify CI, then remove the owned worktree/branch. Run proportionate preview/Git-store/routing/UI tests plus applicable Go, UI build and embed reproducibility checks. This source task does not authorize a live reader replacement.","body":{"branch":"request/source-preview-windows","conditions":"Bounded exact-revision source/evidence windows, real cited-line browser navigation, finite verified reads and safe rendering, producer/consumer controls, architecture/docs, independent review, sealed landing, push/CI and cleanup.","head":"dfbf4089e6826810083848e56e9deff6c0faec29","stale_bases":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:0438e5f5a6b2167feceb5a0c8646280a4227794c, git:sha1:5d2622748872b